title: metarecord:remove
tags: [[GUI command]] Trash
kind: reference
summary: Remove the selected metarecord (its file: trash it, or keep it)

The `Delete` key of the metarecord panels. A metarecord without a file is
deleted (<<cmd "metarecord:delete">>). One with a file asks first, in the
command input (<<cmd "metarecord:remove-file">>): ''trash file'' sends the file to
the trash with its metarecord, ''delete metarecord'' keeps the file and deletes the
metarecord alone, Escape does nothing. Defined in the shipped `commands.js` ([[User commands]]), so its question and its
answers are yours to reshape. See [[Sending files to the trash]].
